WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.625
Here's the comparison, and every rule
on this slide is the kit's own design.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:08.926
It reads each kit run and checks
it against the kit's own manifest:

3
00:00:08.926 --> 00:00:14.363
every listed file with the same hash, nothing
missing, nothing added, and read only.

4
00:00:14.363 --> 00:00:17.563
A run edited after the
kit wrote it is refused.

5
00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:22.983
It also refuses runs from different modes,
clouds or tenants, a run whose manifest

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:27.675
has no tenant ID, and a current run
that isn't later than the previous one.

7
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:33.787
Then it keys each Finding and Warn row by
check, object ID and issue, and sorts it.

8
00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:36.113
New is a row the last run didn't have.

9
00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:40.274
Changed is the same check and object
with a different severity or issue.

10
00:00:40.274 --> 00:00:44.950
Detail only is the same finding with
different detail, and opens nothing.

11
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.275
Resolved is gone from a check
that read the tenant this run.

12
00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:53.500
And unverified is a check that ended in
Error or didn't run: its findings stay open.

13
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.770
Each finding has a fingerprint, so
the tracker never opens a duplicate.
